Package: htheoryR
Title: Hierarchical Entropies (H-Theory) -- Native R Implementation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Raydonal", "Ospina", email = "raydonalmartinez@ufba.br",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9884-9090"))
Description: Native R companion to "Hierarchical entropies" (de Moraes, Brum, Macedo
    and Vasconcelos, Physica A 699 (2026) 131899). Implements the generalized
    statistical factor B_N^(s)(E; a) as a Meijer G-function, the entropy generator
    it inverts to under maximum entropy, and the log-cumulant depth estimator used
    for identifiability and for the mixed-Poisson network application. This is a
    from-scratch R port of the Python package in ../htheory -- see
    data-raw/GOLDEN_PROVENANCE.md for how the two are kept numerically consistent.
